the voyage of the Parker Solar Probe is  about to begin its seven-year mission to  boldly go where no craft has gone before  to touch the Sun to seek out answers to  questions like why is the Sun's corona  so dang hot smaller and speedier than  starships past NASA's Parker Solar Probe  is set to blast off from Cape Canaveral  and aboard a delta 4 heavy rocket the  largest NASA's Arsenal after clearing  Earth's atmosphere Parker will shed its  rocket and get one last boost then  spring-loaded gadgets that were stowed  for launch emerge  solar panels pop out and start charging  the cooling system revs up and antennas  and other instruments stretch out into  space six weeks after launch parker  reaches venus it'll use Venus's gravity  to slingshot itself toward the Sun  another six weeks later Parker becomes  the first spacecraft to enter the sun's  outer atmosphere or Corona the corona is  actually hotter than the surface of the  Sun but a pancake shaped heat shield  keeps all of Parker's gadgets a little  above room temperature most of the  spacecraft's solar panels also tucked  behind the carbon composite shield to  avoid melting traveling at high speeds  will prevent Parker from getting pulled  into the Sun  as the probe surfs the sun's atmosphere  it will gather important intel on solar  radiation electric fields magnetic  fields and particles the data could help  explain what heats up the corona and how  solar wind escapes the Sun and  accelerates through the solar system  [Music]  then Parker swoops back out to cold dark  space and transmits its data back to  earth it'll do the same thing 23 more  times sweeping by the Sun every 88 days  Venus will give the probe six more  slingshot assists and each time it will  inch closer to the sun's surface while  Parker is close to the Sun it won't be  able to radio home so the probe will  have to fly solo tiny solar sensors tell  the craft shimmy left or right when  they're exposed to too much Sun parts of  Parker will get hit with 475 times the  solar radiation that the spacecraft  experienced in orbit around Earth the  probes final three orbits will take it  within six point three million  kilometers of the sun's surface that's  seven times closer than the current  record-holder helios - back in 1976  on its final orbit Parker will also come  in fast and furious at a top speed of  690 thousand kilometers per hour or 190  kilometers per second it'll be the  fastest human-made object in the solar  system at that speed he could travel  from New York to Tokyo in under a minute  so top that Vin Diesel the mission is  set for seven years but it could go  longer whenever Parker meets its end  it'll go out in a blaze of glory once  the probe runs out of fuel most of it  will burn up in the very star it was  said to study but not the heat shield  that giant carbon disc will continue to  orbit the Sun for billions of years  [Music]  [Music]
 

